# Flash Sale Ticketing System — Build Plan

A distributed system that protects your database from a thundering herd of buy requests during a limited-inventory flash sale, by putting Kafka between a bursty, autoscaling API and a small, steady-paced worker that's the *only* thing allowed to touch inventory.

Your original architecture is solid — this doc keeps it intact and adds the handful of pieces (a feedback loop, idempotency, atomic writes, a real load test) needed to make the core claim — *the database stays stable while the API scales* — actually true, and actually provable.

